/T (A core's caches can retain data recently used by a worker. If the worker later executes on another core, some of that cached data may not be available in the same way, increasing memory-access cost. CPU migration is one possible reason for performance changes, but this prototype does not directly count cache misses or migrations unless optional Linux performance counters are collected.)
/E (A core's caches can retain data recently used by a worker. If the worker later executes on another core, some of that cached data may not be available in the same way, increasing memory-access cost. CPU migration is one possible reason for performance changes, but this prototype does not directly count cache misses or migrations unless optional Linux performance counters are collected.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
