/P 113 0 R
/T (4.4 Workload Distribution)
/E (4.4 Workload Distribution)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 113 0 R
/T (Static block distribution assigns contiguous task blocks to workers before execution. It has low coordination overhead, but unequal task costs can create imbalance. Round-robin distribution assigns alternating tasks to workers and can spread expensive tasks more evenly when expensive tasks are distributed through the input sequence. Dynamic distribution lets workers obtain small chunks from a shared queue. It can adapt to unequal task costs, but queue operations introduce coordination overhead.)
/E (Static block distribution assigns contiguous task blocks to workers before execution. It has low coordination overhead, but unequal task costs can create imbalance. Round-robin distribution assigns alternating tasks to workers and can spread expensive tasks more evenly when expensive tasks are distributed through the input sequence. Dynamic distribution lets workers obtain small chunks from a shared queue. It can adapt to unequal task costs, but queue operations introduce coordination overhead.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
