374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 114 0 R
/T (Together, these studies indicate that multi-core performance depends on both where work executes and how work is divided. Affinity can preserve locality and reduce migration, while strict pinning may restrict load balancing. Dynamic work distribution can improve utilization when task costs differ, but coordination overhead can offset the benefit, particularly for small tasks.)
/E (Together, these studies indicate that multi-core performance depends on both where work executes and how work is divided. Affinity can preserve locality and reduce migration, while strict pinning may restrict load balancing. Dynamic work distribution can improve utilization when task costs differ, but coordination overhead can offset the benefit, particularly for small tasks.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
