/Title (This investigation examines how processor affinity and workload distribution influence execution performance on a multi-core Linux system. It defines a controlled CPU-bound workload and compares default scheduling, separate-core pinning and single-core pinning, together with block, round-robin and dynamic task distribution. The prototype measures execution time, throughput, speedup and load imbalance.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1203 0 R
/Next 1270 0 R
>>
