/Title (Modern processors contain multiple CPU cores. The operating-system scheduler decides where runnable processes and threads execute and when they are allowed to run. Good scheduling aims to keep cores usefully occupied while preserving cache locality. Poor placement can leave some cores underused, overload others, or move work between cores and reduce the benefit of cached data.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1339 0 R
/Next 1382 0 R
>>
endobj
